Package: lindos-transfer
Version: 1.0.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), lindos-core (>= 1.0.0)
Recommends: udisks2, ntfs-3g, rsync, zenity, network-manager, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, fontconfig, xdg-user-dirs
Suggests: dislocker, cryptsetup-bin, libldm, python3-yaml, python3-hivex, firefox, lindos-compat, lindos-gaming
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Windows Easy Transfer for Lindos — bring your files and settings over
 lindos-transfer moves what a Windows Easy Transfer wizard would: Desktop,
 Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures, Videos, Saved games, Internet Explorer
 Favorites and OneDrive folders (files stored on this disk only), Chromium and
 Firefox bookmarks, your desktop wallpaper, the fonts you installed yourself,
 Wi-Fi networks, Steam game installs and a list of your Windows programs with
 a Lindos way to get each one back (apt/Flatpak/native browser, a Wine recipe
 or winget install, a web-app shortcut, WinApps/the Windows VM, or an honest
 "not supported on Lindos yet" note with the lindos-game route for anti-cheat
 games, whose publishers decide whether they ever run on Linux).
 .
 Two ways in: the Windows partition of this same PC, mounted strictly
 read-only (never written to, moved or deleted), or a "transfer folder" made
 on the old PC by double-clicking the bundled LindosTransfer.cmd kit — handy
 when Windows is BitLocker-locked, ReFS, a dynamic disk, or already gone.
 .
 lindos-transfer never opens Windows account/security databases, DPAPI keys,
 Credential Manager/Vault, hibernation/page/swap files (beyond a 4 KiB safety
 check) or browser password/cookie stores; it never decrypts BitLocker or
 DPAPI itself (you type the recovery key into udisks/cryptsetup, or into the
 Windows kit); Wi-Fi passwords move only from your own Windows export, on
 through the root helper's stdin, never a command line or a log. Nothing is
 installed or changed without you choosing it first.
 .
 CLI: lindos-transfer (sources, mount, users, plan, run, apps, install-apps,
 make-usb-kit, report). GUI: lindos-transfer-gui (packages/lindos-transfer's
 lindos_transfer.gui, also in this package).
